-- תקנון שירות עובדי הוראה, פרק 6, §6.16 מדריך מקצועי
-- The vocational instructor in a post-primary school: the work unit, the
-- duties and prohibitions of the post, pay for theoretical teaching, the
-- yearly clothing, and the terms of accompanying pupils to industry.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT common

§ `6.16 מדריך מקצועי`

@desc The school calendar the deadlines of section 6.16.3 are counted in, in days. Its figures are inputs; the takanon does not set them here.
DECLARE `instructor calendar` HAS
    `days in a term`                        IS A NUMBER @desc a שליש
    `days counted as the start of the year` IS A NUMBER @desc "בראשית שנת הלימודים"

DECLARE `instructor action` IS ONE OF
    `perform` HAS `the duty` IS A `instructor duty`
    `do` HAS `the forbidden act` IS A `forbidden act`
    `be ready in the workshop`
    `notify the principal of an absence`
    `assign the instructor's classes and subjects`

@desc The instructor's duties, in the order of section 6.16.3's paragraphs.
DECLARE `instructor duty` IS ONE OF
    `imparting the trade, correct work habits and love of work to his pupils, by planned and directed means and by personal example`
    `instructing each subject by the general curriculum or by a special one approved for the school he works in`
    `submitting for the principal's approval the plan dividing his work for each term, and the lesson plans`
    `planning each lesson to the subject's didactic demands`
    `accompanying his instruction and the practical work with suitable explanations, and educating his pupils for responsibility and safety at work and for care of the materials and tools`
    `submitting to the principal a detailed written report on carrying out the curriculum`
    `reporting to the principal that the curriculum was not carried out in full, and explaining why`
    `reporting to the principal, routinely through the year, every fault in carrying out the work plan`
    `keeping a regular work diary of the instruction material and work, the drawings and notes he prepared and the technological explanations he gave`
    `keeping the class register and seeing that the pupils fill in their workbooks properly`
    `giving the principal in writing the grades he set, at the times and by the arrangements of the institution`
    `giving the principal general assessments of each pupil's achievements`
    `keeping written and oral records of the pupils' achievements as the basis for the grades, and putting them at the principal's disposal on request`
    `keeping the registers and books our Ministry and the owner require, and seeing to the records they require`
    `doing his utmost to take part in the pupils' promotion examinations, by the arrangements the school management sets`
    `attending every meeting of the pedagogical council`
    `attending any other meeting the principal invites him to`
    `taking part in the duty rosters the principal sets to supervise the pupils on school grounds before lessons, in breaks and after lessons`
    `answering the principal's demand to substitute for missing teachers or instructors`
    `being at school in those hours, at the principal's disposal, and substituting for missing teachers or instructors as needed, without pay`
    `helping, in his free hours, with substitution by teaching his subjects or supervising the pupils`
    `receiving parents and pupils one hour a week outside his regular working hours`
    `setting times to receive parents and pupils as needed`
    `starting and ending the workshop lesson with the bell`
    `answering for the equipment, its proper upkeep, and the furniture, tools and materials given to him, and making running repairs as far as possible, also with the pupils' help`
    `ensuring his department has the safety means and conditions the binding instructions require, and that his pupils keep every safety rule`
    `carrying out the preparations needed for arrangements and summaries`
    `referring the pupil to the class educator or the school management`
    `training in his free time (in the school year, the holidays and the annual vacations) in the in-service training our Ministry, the local education authorities and other owners run`

@desc What the instructor must not do (section 6.16.3), each with its exception.
DECLARE `forbidden act` IS ONE OF
    `lowering a grade in the subjects of study as a means of punishing a pupil`
    `giving a person who is not a member of the pedagogical council any details of its deliberations, save with the principal's consent`
    `giving any certificate or document that may be seen as given on the school's behalf, save with the principal's consent`
    `giving any details about his pupils to anyone but the principal, the class educator, the parents or the guardians`
    `inviting outside guests or visitors to the school or his class, save with the principal's approval`
    `inflicting any corporal punishment, in any case`

GIVEN d IS A `instructor duty`, why IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `instructor action`
DECIDE `the instructor must` d why IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `perform` done PROVIDED done EQUALS d
    LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE why

GIVEN d IS A `instructor duty`, days IS A NUMBER, why IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `instructor action`
DECIDE `the instructor must, in time,` d days why IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `perform` done PROVIDED done EQUALS d
    WITHIN days
    LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE why

GIVEN f IS A `forbidden act`, why IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `instructor action`
DECIDE `the instructor shall not` f why IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    SHANT `do` act PROVIDED act EQUALS f
    LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE why

@desc A vocational instructor's employment, as far as section 6.16.5 asks.
DECLARE `instructor employment` HAS
    `is a certified vocational instructor` IS A BOOLEAN @desc of the grade "מדריך מקצועי מוסמך"
    `teaches in the middle or upper division the theoretical subjects he is certified in` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an academic vocational instructor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is employed in vocational instruction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is employed in theoretical teaching`   IS A BOOLEAN

@desc One year's clothing under section 6.16.6.
DECLARE `instructor clothing` HAS
    `pairs of shoes`            IS A NUMBER
    `pairs of high white shoes` IS A NUMBER
    `coats`                     IS A NUMBER

`no clothing` MEANS `instructor clothing` WITH `pairs of shoes` IS 0, `pairs of high white shoes` IS 0, `coats` IS 0

@desc A person section 6.16.6 may give clothing to.
DECLARE `clothing claimant` HAS
    `is a vocational instructor`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a teacher in the track`               IS A BOOLEAN @desc a teacher (not an instructor) in the nursing, dental-technician or dental-assistant track, for section 6.16.6ד
    `trade`                                   IS A `vocational trade`
    `must wear high white shoes in hospitals` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a woman`                              IS A BOOLEAN @desc 6.16.6ד.1 gives the shoes to "מורות" (women teachers)

DECLARE `laundry payer` IS ONE OF `the institution`, `the instructor`

§§ `6.16.1 יחידת עבודה`

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_1__para_1
`a vocational instructor's work unit in a post-primary school, in weekly hours` MEANS 24

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_1/p1 akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_1/p2 The sources (אסמכתא) of section 6.16.1.

§§ `6.16.3 הגדרת תפקידים`

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_1
GIVEN `the duty accords with his instruction licence from the Ministry` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the instructor is employed in that instruction duty in the vocational school` `the duty accords with his instruction licence from the Ministry` IF
    `the duty accords with his instruction licence from the Ministry`

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_2
`6.16.3.2 imparting the trade` MEANS
    `the instructor must` `imparting the trade, correct work habits and love of work to his pupils, by planned and directed means and by personal example` "6.16.3.2"

-- 3: the instructor's work arrangement in the school, both the classes and
-- the subjects, is in the principal's hands.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_3
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `instructor action`
DECIDE `6.16.3.3 arranging the instructor's work` IS
    PARTY `the school principal`
    MAY   `assign the instructor's classes and subjects`

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_4
`6.16.3.4 the curriculum` MEANS
    `the instructor must` `instructing each subject by the general curriculum or by a special one approved for the school he works in` "6.16.3.4"

-- 5א: at the start of the school year, mindful of how the year is divided
-- and of the yearly curriculum.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_5__subpara_a
GIVEN c IS A `instructor calendar`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `instructor action`
DECIDE `6.16.3.5א the work plan` c IS
    `the instructor must, in time,` `submitting for the principal's approval the plan dividing his work for each term, and the lesson plans` (c's `days counted as the start of the year`) "6.16.3.5א: the plans are submitted at the start of the school year"
    RAND `the instructor must` `planning each lesson to the subject's didactic demands` "6.16.3.5א"

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_5__subpara_b
`6.16.3.5ב explanation and safety` MEANS
    `the instructor must` `accompanying his instruction and the practical work with suitable explanations, and educating his pupils for responsibility and safety at work and for care of the materials and tools` "6.16.3.5ב"

-- 6: at the end of each term a detailed written report; if the curriculum
-- was not carried out in full, for whatever reason, he reports it and
-- explains why; and through the year he reports every fault as it arises.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_6
GIVEN c IS A `instructor calendar`, `the curriculum was carried out in full` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `instructor action`
DECIDE `6.16.3.6 reporting` c `the curriculum was carried out in full` IS
    `the instructor must, in time,` `submitting to the principal a detailed written report on carrying out the curriculum` (c's `days in a term`) "6.16.3.6: the report is submitted at the end of each term"
    RAND (IF `the curriculum was carried out in full`
          THEN FULFILLED
          ELSE `the instructor must` `reporting to the principal that the curriculum was not carried out in full, and explaining why` "6.16.3.6")
    RAND `the instructor must` `reporting to the principal, routinely through the year, every fault in carrying out the work plan` "6.16.3.6"

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_7
`6.16.3.7 the work diary` MEANS
    `the instructor must` `keeping a regular work diary of the instruction material and work, the drawings and notes he prepared and the technological explanations he gave` "6.16.3.7"
    RAND `the instructor must` `keeping the class register and seeing that the pupils fill in their workbooks properly` "6.16.3.7"

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_8__subpara_a
GIVEN `the principal asks for assessments` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `instructor action`
DECIDE `6.16.3.8א grades` `the principal asks for assessments` IS
    `the instructor must` `giving the principal in writing the grades he set, at the times and by the arrangements of the institution` "6.16.3.8א"
    RAND (IF `the principal asks for assessments`
          THEN `the instructor must` `giving the principal general assessments of each pupil's achievements` "6.16.3.8א: on the principal's request"
          ELSE FULFILLED)

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_8__subpara_b
`6.16.3.8ב records` MEANS
    `the instructor must` `keeping written and oral records of the pupils' achievements as the basis for the grades, and putting them at the principal's disposal on request` "6.16.3.8ב"
    RAND `the instructor must` `keeping the registers and books our Ministry and the owner require, and seeing to the records they require` "6.16.3.8ב"

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_9
`6.16.3.9 no grade as punishment` MEANS
    `the instructor shall not` `lowering a grade in the subjects of study as a means of punishing a pupil` "6.16.3.9"

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_10
`6.16.3.10 promotion examinations` MEANS
    `the instructor must` `doing his utmost to take part in the pupils' promotion examinations, by the arrangements the school management sets` "6.16.3.10"

-- 11: as a member of the pedagogical council he attends all its meetings,
-- and any other meeting the principal invites him to.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_11
GIVEN `invited by the principal to another meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `instructor action`
DECIDE `6.16.3.11 meetings` `invited by the principal to another meeting` IS
    `the instructor must` `attending every meeting of the pedagogical council` "6.16.3.11: the instructor is a member of the pedagogical council"
    RAND (IF `invited by the principal to another meeting`
          THEN `the instructor must` `attending any other meeting the principal invites him to` "6.16.3.11"
          ELSE FULFILLED)

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_12
`6.16.3.12 duty rosters` MEANS
    `the instructor must` `taking part in the duty rosters the principal sets to supervise the pupils on school grounds before lessons, in breaks and after lessons` "6.16.3.12"

-- 13: on the principal's demand he substitutes, to prevent lost lessons; an
-- instructor freed on a day by the pupils' trip, work camp and the like is
-- at school in those hours and substitutes as needed, without pay; other
-- instructors help in their free hours.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_13
GIVEN `the principal demands a substitution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `freed that day because the pupils are on a trip, at a work camp or the like` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `instructor action`
DECIDE `6.16.3.13 substitution` `the principal demands a substitution` `freed that day because the pupils are on a trip, at a work camp or the like` IS
    (IF `the principal demands a substitution`
     THEN `the instructor must` `answering the principal's demand to substitute for missing teachers or instructors` "6.16.3.13: to prevent lost lessons and keep the school's studies in order"
     ELSE FULFILLED)
    RAND (IF `freed that day because the pupils are on a trip, at a work camp or the like`
          THEN `the instructor must` `being at school in those hours, at the principal's disposal, and substituting for missing teachers or instructors as needed, without pay` "6.16.3.13: the instructor freed by the pupils' absence"
          ELSE `the instructor must` `helping, in his free hours, with substitution by teaching his subjects or supervising the pupils` "6.16.3.13: the other instructors")

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_14__subpara_a akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_14__subpara_b
GIVEN `is a class educator` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `instructor action`
DECIDE `6.16.3.14 receiving parents and pupils` `is a class educator` IS
    IF `is a class educator`
    THEN `the instructor must, in time,` `receiving parents and pupils one hour a week outside his regular working hours` 7 "6.16.3.14א: one hour every week"
    ELSE `the instructor must` `setting times to receive parents and pupils as needed` "6.16.3.14ב"

-- 15: in the workshop, ready for work, at least 5 minutes before the bell.
-- Time in minutes from when the instructor's day starts.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_15
GIVEN `minutes until the bell` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `instructor action`
DECIDE `6.16.3.15 ready before the bell` `minutes until the bell` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `be ready in the workshop`
    WITHIN `minutes until the bell` MINUS 5
    LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "6.16.3.15: in the workshop, ready for work, at least 5 minutes before the bell"

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_16
`6.16.3.16 the bell` MEANS
    `the instructor must` `starting and ending the workshop lesson with the bell` "6.16.3.16"

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_17
`6.16.3.17 equipment` MEANS
    `the instructor must` `answering for the equipment, its proper upkeep, and the furniture, tools and materials given to him, and making running repairs as far as possible, also with the pupils' help` "6.16.3.17"

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_18
`6.16.3.18 safety` MEANS
    `the instructor must` `ensuring his department has the safety means and conditions the binding instructions require, and that his pupils keep every safety rule` "6.16.3.18"

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_19
`6.16.3.19 preparations` MEANS
    `the instructor must` `carrying out the preparations needed for arrangements and summaries` "6.16.3.19"

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_20
`6.16.3.20 the council and the school's documents` MEANS
    `the instructor shall not` `giving a person who is not a member of the pedagogical council any details of its deliberations, save with the principal's consent` "6.16.3.20"
    RAND `the instructor shall not` `giving any certificate or document that may be seen as given on the school's behalf, save with the principal's consent` "6.16.3.20"

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_21
`6.16.3.21 details about pupils` MEANS
    `the instructor shall not` `giving any details about his pupils to anyone but the principal, the class educator, the parents or the guardians` "6.16.3.21"

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_22
`6.16.3.22 outside guests` MEANS
    `the instructor shall not` `inviting outside guests or visitors to the school or his class, save with the principal's approval` "6.16.3.22"

-- 23: an instructor prevented by illness or another justified reason, who
-- must be absent, tells the principal as soon as possible and at the latest
-- on the morning of the first day of absence, before lessons start. Time in
-- hours from when the instructor knows of it.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_23
GIVEN `hours until lessons start on the first day of absence` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `instructor action`
DECIDE `6.16.3.23 reporting an absence` `hours until lessons start on the first day of absence` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `notify the principal of an absence`
    WITHIN `hours until lessons start on the first day of absence`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "6.16.3.23: an absence is reported as soon as possible, and before lessons start on its first day at the latest"

-- 24: no corporal punishment in any case; a pupil whose grave breach of
-- discipline in the lesson calls for removing him from the workshop is
-- referred to the class educator or the school management, who act by the
-- regulations.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_24
GIVEN `a grave breach of discipline in his lesson calls for removing a pupil from the workshop` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `instructor action`
DECIDE `6.16.3.24 discipline` `a grave breach of discipline in his lesson calls for removing a pupil from the workshop` IS
    `the instructor shall not` `inflicting any corporal punishment, in any case` "6.16.3.24"
    RAND (IF `a grave breach of discipline in his lesson calls for removing a pupil from the workshop`
          THEN `the instructor must` `referring the pupil to the class educator or the school management` "6.16.3.24: they act by the regulations"
          ELSE FULFILLED)

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3__para_25
`6.16.3.25 in-service training` MEANS
    `the instructor must` `training in his free time (in the school year, the holidays and the annual vacations) in the in-service training our Ministry, the local education authorities and other owners run` "6.16.3.25"

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3/p1 akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_3/p2 The source (אסמכתא) of section 6.16.3.

§§ `6.16.5 שכר להוראה`

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_5__para_1
GIVEN e IS A `instructor employment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paid by his grade as a certified vocational instructor` e IF
        e's `is a certified vocational instructor`
    AND e's `teaches in the middle or upper division the theoretical subjects he is certified in`

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_5__para_2
GIVEN e IS A `instructor employment`, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `paid both as instructor and as teacher by the academic teachers' scale (BA, MA or doctor)` e `the day` IF
        e's `is an academic vocational instructor`
    AND e's `is employed in vocational instruction`
    AND e's `is employed in theoretical teaching`
    AND `the academic arrangement is in force on` `the day`

-- §6.16.5.2 runs from the start of 5734 (1.9.1973).
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_5__para_2/p2
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the academic arrangement is in force on` `the day` IF
    `the day` AT LEAST Date 1 9 1973

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_5/p1 akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_5/p2 akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_5/p3 The sources (אסמכתא) of section 6.16.5.

§§ `6.16.6 קצובת ביגוד`

@desc The trades of section 6.16.6א and ב, one per paragraph, and the tracks of 6.16.6ד.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_a/p1
DECLARE `vocational trade` IS ONE OF
    `mechanics`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_a__subpara_2
    `metalwork, piping and structures`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_a__subpara_3
    `motor mechanics`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_a__subpara_4
    `motor electrics`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_a__subpara_5
    `aircraft mechanics`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_a__subpara_6
    `agricultural machinery`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_a__subpara_7
    `marine mechanics`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_a__subpara_8
    `equipment and ground mechanics`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_a__subpara_9
    `electricity`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_a__subpara_10
    `refrigeration and air conditioning`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_a__subpara_11
    `woodworking`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_a__subpara_12
    `cookery`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_a__subpara_13
    `printing`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_a__subpara_14
    `deckhands`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_a__subpara_15
    `building: building site`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_a__subpara_16
    `photography`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_a__subpara_17
    `ceramics`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_b__subpara_1
    `instrumentation and control`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_b__subpara_2
    `electronics`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_b__subpara_3
    `automatic data processing`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_b__subpara_4
    `hospitality and housekeeping`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_b__subpara_5
    `nursery nurses`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_b__subpara_6
    `industrial laboratory technicians`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_b__subpara_7
    `laboratory technicians for schools`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_b__subpara_8
    `literature`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_b__subpara_9
    `applied art`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_b__subpara_10
    `fashion`
    @ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_b__subpara_11
    `nursing`
    `dental technicians`
    `dental assistants`
    `another trade`

-- The first trade's own paragraph (א.1) is cited with the list it opens.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_a/p1 akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_a__subpara_1
`the shoes-and-two-coats trades` MEANS
    LIST `mechanics`, `metalwork, piping and structures`, `motor mechanics`, `motor electrics`,
         `aircraft mechanics`, `agricultural machinery`, `marine mechanics`,
         `equipment and ground mechanics`, `electricity`, `refrigeration and air conditioning`,
         `woodworking`, `cookery`, `printing`, `deckhands`, `building: building site`,
         `photography`, `ceramics`

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_b/p1
`the two-coats trades` MEANS
    LIST `instrumentation and control`, `electronics`, `automatic data processing`,
         `hospitality and housekeeping`, `nursery nurses`, `industrial laboratory technicians`,
         `laboratory technicians for schools`, `literature`, `applied art`, `fashion`, `nursing`

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_a/p1 akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_b/p1
GIVEN c IS A `clothing claimant`
GIVETH A `instructor clothing`
DECIDE `an instructor's clothing` c IS
    BRANCH
        IF c's `is a vocational instructor` AND elem (c's `trade`) `the shoes-and-two-coats trades`
        THEN `instructor clothing` WITH `pairs of shoes` IS 1, `pairs of high white shoes` IS 0, `coats` IS 2
        IF c's `is a vocational instructor` AND elem (c's `trade`) `the two-coats trades`
        THEN `instructor clothing` WITH `pairs of shoes` IS 0, `pairs of high white shoes` IS 0, `coats` IS 2
        OTHERWISE `no clothing`

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_c
`who pays for laundering the coats` MEANS `the institution`

-- F-6.16-a: "התחולה: 1 בספטמבר 1982" is printed under ד.2 alone, and
-- nothing says whether it dates ד.2 or the whole of ד. The reading adopted:
-- the whole of ד, the date closing the paragraph (ד.1 carries no date of
-- its own).
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_d__subpara_1 akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_d__subpara_2 akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6__para_d__subpara_2/p2
GIVEN c IS A `clothing claimant`, `the year begins on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `instructor clothing`
DECIDE `a track teacher's clothing` c `the year begins on` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (c's `is a teacher in the track` AND `the year begins on` AT LEAST Date 1 9 1982)
        THEN `no clothing`
        IF c's `trade` EQUALS `nursing` AND c's `is a woman` AND c's `must wear high white shoes in hospitals`
        THEN `instructor clothing` WITH `pairs of shoes` IS 0, `pairs of high white shoes` IS 1, `coats` IS 0
        IF c's `trade` EQUALS `dental technicians` OR c's `trade` EQUALS `dental assistants`
        THEN `instructor clothing` WITH `pairs of shoes` IS 0, `pairs of high white shoes` IS 0, `coats` IS 2
        OTHERWISE `no clothing`

-- The other reading of F-6.16-a: the date dates ד.2 alone, and ד.1 has no
-- start date.
GIVEN c IS A `clothing claimant`, `the year begins on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `instructor clothing`
DECIDE `a track teacher's clothing, the date dating ד.2 alone` c `the year begins on` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT c's `is a teacher in the track`
        THEN `no clothing`
        IF c's `trade` EQUALS `nursing` AND c's `is a woman` AND c's `must wear high white shoes in hospitals`
        THEN `instructor clothing` WITH `pairs of shoes` IS 0, `pairs of high white shoes` IS 1, `coats` IS 0
        IF (c's `trade` EQUALS `dental technicians` OR c's `trade` EQUALS `dental assistants`)
           AND `the year begins on` AT LEAST Date 1 9 1982
        THEN `instructor clothing` WITH `pairs of shoes` IS 0, `pairs of high white shoes` IS 0, `coats` IS 2
        OTHERWISE `no clothing`

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6/p1 akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6/p2 akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6/p3 akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_6/p4 The sources (אסמכתא) of section 6.16.6.

§§ `6.16.7 ליווי תלמידים לתעשייה`

@desc An arrangement for accompanying pupils to work in industry.
@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_7/p1
DECLARE `industry escort` HAS
    `escort is an instructor of the pupils' own trade`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `school workshops are kept free for the pupils' return`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `work groups kept as they are, flexibly`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `escorting rotates among the instructors`                IS A BOOLEAN

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_7__para_1 akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_7__para_2 akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_7__para_4 akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_7__para_5
GIVEN e IS A `industry escort`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the escort meets the conditions` e IF
        e's `escort is an instructor of the pupils' own trade`
    AND e's `school workshops are kept free for the pupils' return`
    AND e's `work groups kept as they are, flexibly`
    AND e's `escorting rotates among the instructors`

@ref akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_7__para_3
GIVEN `hours in industry` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `workshop hours counted` `hours in industry` IS
    `hours in industry`

-- akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_7/p2 akn:chp_6__sec_6_16__ssec_6_16_7/p3 The source (אסמכתא) of section 6.16.7.

§§ `Worked examples`

-- Examples. The calendar's figures are placeholders.
`a placeholder calendar` MEANS
    `instructor calendar` WITH
        `days in a term`                        IS 100
        `days counted as the start of the year` IS 30

`a motor mechanics instructor` MEANS
    `clothing claimant` WITH
        `is a vocational instructor`              IS TRUE
        `is a teacher in the track`               IS FALSE
        `trade`                                   IS `motor mechanics`
        `must wear high white shoes in hospitals` IS FALSE
        `is a woman`                              IS FALSE

`a nursing-track teacher in 1981` MEANS
    `clothing claimant` WITH
        `is a vocational instructor`              IS FALSE
        `is a teacher in the track`               IS TRUE
        `trade`                                   IS `nursing`
        `must wear high white shoes in hospitals` IS TRUE
        `is a woman`                              IS TRUE

-- F-6.16-a's evidence: the two readings of ד's start date give a nursing
-- teacher different shoes for a year beginning 1.9.1981.
`the two readings of ד's start date differ` MEANS
    NOT (`a track teacher's clothing` `a nursing-track teacher in 1981` (Date 1 9 1981)
         EQUALS `a track teacher's clothing, the date dating ד.2 alone` `a nursing-track teacher in 1981` (Date 1 9 1981))
#ASSERT `the two readings of ד's start date differ`

`an academic instructor who also teaches theory` MEANS
    `instructor employment` WITH
        `is a certified vocational instructor` IS FALSE
        `teaches in the middle or upper division the theoretical subjects he is certified in` IS FALSE
        `is an academic vocational instructor` IS TRUE
        `is employed in vocational instruction` IS TRUE
        `is employed in theoretical teaching`   IS TRUE

#ASSERT `an instructor's clothing` `a motor mechanics instructor` EQUALS `instructor clothing` WITH `pairs of shoes` IS 1, `pairs of high white shoes` IS 0, `coats` IS 2
#ASSERT `paid both as instructor and as teacher by the academic teachers' scale (BA, MA or doctor)` `an academic instructor who also teaches theory` (Date 1 9 1990)
#ASSERT NOT `paid both as instructor and as teacher by the academic teachers' scale (BA, MA or doctor)` `an academic instructor who also teaches theory` (Date 1 9 1972)
#ASSERT NOT `paid by his grade as a certified vocational instructor` `an academic instructor who also teaches theory`

-- A class educator's weekly reception hour, held on day 3: fulfilled.
-- Corporal punishment: the prohibition is breached. Ready 6 minutes before
-- a bell 30 minutes away: fulfilled; 2 minutes after the bell: breached.
#TRACE `6.16.3.14 receiving parents and pupils` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `perform` `receiving parents and pupils one hour a week outside his regular working hours` AT 3
#TRACE `6.16.3.24 discipline` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `do` `inflicting any corporal punishment, in any case` AT 5
#TRACE `6.16.3.15 ready before the bell` 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `be ready in the workshop` AT 24
#TRACE `6.16.3.15 ready before the bell` 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `be ready in the workshop` AT 32
#TRACE `6.16.3.23 reporting an absence` 14 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `notify the principal of an absence` AT 2
#TRACE `6.16.3.5א the work plan` `a placeholder calendar` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `perform` `submitting for the principal's approval the plan dividing his work for each term, and the lesson plans` AT 10
